{"name":"Indigo Batik","hex":"#4467a7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"indigo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A purplish-blue color.","A greenish dark blue color; the color of indigo dye."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["having a deep purplish-blue colour"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indigo"},{"term":"batik","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A wax-resist method of dyeing fabric."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To dye fabric using the wax-resist method."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/batik"}],"entries":[{"title":"Indigo","blocks":[{"text":"Indigo is a term used for a number of hues in the region of blue. The word comes from the ancient dye of the same name. The term \"indigo\" can refer to the color of the dye, various colors of fabric dyed with indigo dye, a spectral color, one of the seven colors of the rainbow as described by Sir Isaac Newton, or a region on the color wheel, and can include various shades of blue, ultramarine, and green-blue. Since the web era, the term has also been used for various purple and violet hues identified as \"indigo\", based on use of the term \"indigo\" in HTML web page specifications."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Indian_indigo_dye_lump.jpg/330px-Indian_indigo_dye_lump.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigo","wikidata":"Q5967009"},{"title":"Batik","blocks":[{"text":"Batik is a dyeing technique using wax resist. The term is also used to describe patterned textiles created with that technique. Batik is made by drawing or stamping wax on a cloth to prevent colour absorption during the dyeing process. This creates a patterned negative when the wax is removed from the dyed cloth. Artisans may create intricate coloured patterns with multiple cycles of wax application and dyeing. Patterns and motifs vary widely even within countries. Some patterns hold symbolic significance and are used only in certain occasions, while others were created to satisfy market demand and fashion trends."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Batik_Trusmi_Cirebon_%2823%29.jpg/330px-Batik_Trusmi_Cirebon_%2823%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batik","wikidata":"Q635427"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Passerina_cyanea_Sam_Smith_Park_Toronto.jpg/500px-Passerina_cyanea_Sam_Smith_Park_Toronto.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Passerina_cyanea_Sam_Smith_Park_Toronto.jpg/500px-Passerina_cyanea_Sam_Smith_Park_Toronto.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APasserina_cyanea_Sam_Smith_Park_Toronto.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Lactarius_indigo_%28Schwein.%29_Fr_939963.jpg/500px-Lactarius_indigo_%28Schwein.%29_Fr_939963.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Lactarius_indigo_%28Schwein.%29_Fr_939963.jpg/500px-Lactarius_indigo_%28Schwein.%29_Fr_939963.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALactarius_indigo_(Schwein.)_Fr_939963.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/1923ca_Quarter_anna_Bundi_indigo_SG26a_Mi18.jpg/500px-1923ca_Quarter_anna_Bundi_indigo_SG26a_Mi18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/1923ca_Quarter_anna_Bundi_indigo_SG26a_Mi18.jpg/500px-1923ca_Quarter_anna_Bundi_indigo_SG26a_Mi18.jpg?utm